-- title:
--   Flatness of adic completion along a flat finite-type map
-- statement:
--   Let $B_0$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and let $B$ be a commutative $B_0$-algebra (in the same universe) which is flat as a $B_0$-module and of finite type as a $B_0$-algebra, and let $I_0 \subseteq B_0$ be an ideal. Write $\widehat{B_0}$ for the $I_0$-adic completion `AdicCompletion I₀ B₀` of $B_0$, let $I_0B$ denote the ideal `I₀.map (algebraMap B₀ B)` of $B$ generated by the image of $I_0$, and write $\widehat{B}$ for the $I_0B$-adic completion of $B$. The assertion is that there exists a ring homomorphism $f : \widehat{B_0} \to \widehat{B}$ such that (i) for every $b \in B_0$, $f$ applied to the canonical image of $b$ in $\widehat{B_0}$ equals the canonical image in $\widehat{B}$ of the image of $b$ in $B$, i.e. the square formed by $f$, the two completion maps and $B_0 \to B$ commutes; and (ii) with the $\widehat{B_0}$-algebra structure on $\widehat{B}$ given by $f$, the module $\widehat{B}$ is flat over $\widehat{B_0}$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that adic completion is compatible with, and preserves flatness under, a flat finite-type extension of Noetherian rings: $\widehat{B}$ is flat over $\widehat{B_0}$ for the completion of the base ideal. It is used in the deformation-theoretic part of the development, through a statement on $\mathcal{O}$-module presheaves and proper morphisms ([`AlgebraicGeometry.OModulePresheaf.exists_forall_thread_smul_eq_apply_and_smul_eq_zero_of_isIso_pullback_snd_of_isProper`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.OModulePresheaf.exists_forall_thread_smul_eq_apply_and_smul_eq_zero_of_isIso_pullback_snd_of_isProper)).
